# Deployment Guide

This guide covers deploying the boilerplate with Docker and Cloudflare Tunnel.

## Prerequisites

- Docker and Docker Compose
- Cloudflare account with a domain
- Bun (for frontend build)

## Quick Start

### 1. Clone and Configure

```bash
# Clone the boilerplate
git clone <your-repo> my-app
cd my-app

# Copy environment template
cp .env.example .env
```

### 2. Configure Environment

Edit `.env`:

```bash
{% if include_auth %}
JWT_SECRET=your-secure-random-string
{% endif %}
SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com
DATABASE_URL={% if database == 'sqlite' %}sqlite+aiosqlite:///{% else %}{{ package_name }}.db{% endif %}
```

Generate a secure JWT secret:
```bash
openssl rand -hex 32
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
# Install Python dependencies
pdm install

# Install Node dependencies
pdm run client_install

# Build frontend assets
pdm run build
```

### 4. Run Database Migrations

```bash
pdm run migrate
```

### 5. Build and Run with Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build -d
```

The app will be available at `http://localhost:{{ port }}`

## Production Deployment

### Set Up Cloudflare Tunnel

Run these commands once to expose your app to the internet:

```bash
# Set ownership for cloudflared directory
sudo chown 65532:65532 .cloudflare

# Login to Cloudflare (opens browser)
docker compose run --rm cloudflare tunnel login

# Create tunnel
docker compose run --rm cloudflare tunnel create {{ package_name }}

# Create DNS records for domain and www
docker compose run --rm cloudflare tunnel route dns {{ package_name }} {{ site_host }}
docker compose run --rm cloudflare tunnel route dns {{ package_name }} www.{{ site_host }}
```

[Extract Tunnel Credentials](#extract-tunnel-credentials) to create the credentials file.

### Start Services

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Your app will be available at `https://{{ site_host }}`

## Adding New Features

### Create a New Feature

```bash
# Copy the hello feature as a template
cp -r src/{{ package_name }}/features/hello src/{{ package_name }}/features/your_feature

# Update the files:
# - models.py (your database models)
# - services.py (database queries)
# - routes.py (API endpoints)
# - templates/*.html (your UI)
```

### Register the Feature

In `src/{{ package_name }}/app.py`:

```python
from {{ package_name }}.features.your_feature.routes import router as your_feature_router

# Add to app
app.include_router(your_feature_router)
```

### Add Frontend Assets

In `vite.config.js`, add your entry point:

```javascript
input: {
  main: './src/{{ package_name }}/core/client/main.ts',
  hello: './src/{{ package_name }}/features/hello/client/main.ts',
  your_feature: './src/{{ package_name }}/features/your_feature/client/main.ts',
}
```

