## Troubleshooting

### App Won't Start

Check logs:
```bash
docker-compose logs app
```

### Database Issues

Reset the database:
```bash
docker-compose exec app pdm run drop_db
docker-compose exec app pdm run migrate
```

### Tunnel Connection Issues

Check tunnel logs:
```bash
docker-compose logs cloudflare
```

Verify credentials:
```bash
ls -la .cloudflare/
```

## Reference

### Extract Tunnel Credentials

```bash
TUNNEL_NAME={{ package_name }}
docker compose run --rm cloudflare tunnel token $TUNNEL_NAME \
  | base64 --decode \
  | jq '
    .AccountTag = .a
    | .TunnelSecret = .s
    | .TunnelID = .t
    | .Endpoint = ""
    | del(.a, .s, .t)
  ' \
  | tee >(jq -r '.TunnelID' | xargs -I{} sh -c "cat > '.cloudflare/{}.json'") >/dev/null
```

This creates `{tunnel-id}.json` in the `.cloudflare` directory.

### Update Config with Tunnel ID

```bash
TUNNEL_ID=$(jq -r '.TunnelID' .cloudflare/*.json)
sed -i "s/\[\[tunnel-id\]\]/$TUNNEL_ID/g" .cloudflare/config.yml.jinja
```

### Backup: Restore Tunnel Credentials

If the credentials file is lost, run [Extract Tunnel Credentials](#extract-tunnel-credentials) then run [Update Config with Tunnel ID](#update-config-with-tunnel-id).
